# Atomic Design

Classify before adding a file. New UI goes in one layer under `frontend/components/`. Routes in `frontend/pages/` are the page layer. `frontend/components/layouts/` is legacy; new screen layouts go in `templates`. Do not mass-move `navbar` or `footer`.

| Layer | Folder | May import |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Atom | `components/atoms` | Native elements only |
| Molecule | `components/molecules` | Atoms |
| Organism | `components/organisms` | Molecules, atoms |
| Template | `components/templates` | Organisms, molecules, atoms |
| Page | `pages/` | Its template, plus data loading |

Imports point downward only. Fetching and route data stay in the page and go through `frontend/services/httpService.ts`. Atoms, molecules, organisms, and templates receive props and callbacks. They do not call HTTP.

```tsx
// page loads data and fills one template
const profile = await http.get("/api/profile");
return <ProfileTemplate profile={profile} />;
```

One component per file. Name it for what it is. Do not put the layer in the name. Create a layer folder only when the first component of that layer is added.
